<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Description>DuckDB Bindings for C#.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
- Updated to DuckDB v2.0.1

Upgrading from 1.x: https://duckdb.net/docs/upgrade-to-2.0.html
All changes: https://duckdb.net/docs/release-notes/2.0.html

New features:
- DuckDBHugeInt and DuckDBUHugeInt can be created from an Int128 and a UInt128
- DuckDBType has the DuckDB 1.5 types STRING_LITERAL, INTEGER_LITERAL, TIME_NS, GEOMETRY and VARIANT
- A DuckDBCreateVarchar overload for UTF-8 bytes, which keeps NUL characters
- Bindings for duckdb_prepared_statement_type, duckdb_clear_bindings, duckdb_create_varchar_length, duckdb_schema_from_arrow, duckdb_data_chunk_from_arrow and duckdb_destroy_arrow_converted_schema

Breaking changes:
- DuckDB.NET.Bindings 2.0 needs DuckDB.NET.Data 2.0. DuckDB.NET.Data 1.x with Bindings 2.0 throws TypeLoadException at the first string append, so upgrade both packages together
- DuckDBString.value and the nested type DuckDBString._value_e__Union are removed. Read a string with Length and Data, and build a short one with DuckDBString.TryCreateInlined. DuckDBStringInlined is internal
- NativeMethods.Value.DuckDBCreateVarchar takes a non-nullable string. Use DuckDBCreateNullValue for NULL
- DuckDBValue.GetValue&lt;T&gt; gives the value as its own type, as object, a nullable of it or an interface it implements, and throws InvalidCastException for any other T. It reinterpreted the value's memory as T. A HUGEINT or UHUGEINT is an Int128 or UInt128 unless T is BigInteger

Fixes:
- Some native function declarations were corrected to match duckdb.h
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <RootNamespace>DuckDB.NET.Native</RootNamespace>
    <RuntimeIdentifiers>win-x64;win-arm64;linux-x64;linux-arm64;osx</RuntimeIdentifiers>
    <DuckDbArtifactRoot Condition=" '$(DuckDbArtifactRoot)' == '' ">https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/releases/download/v2.0.1</DuckDbArtifactRoot>
    <SignAssembly>True</SignAssembly>
    <AssemblyOriginatorKeyFile>..\keyPair.snk</AssemblyOriginatorKeyFile>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(BuildType)' == 'ManagedOnly' ">
    <Description>$(Description) $(NoNativeText)</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>
  
  <!-- Download and include the native libraries into the NuGet package-->
  <Target Name="DownloadNativeLibs" BeforeTargets="GenerateAdditionalSources" Condition="'$(BuildType)' == 'Full' AND '$(TargetFramework)' == '$([System.String]::Copy($(TargetFrameworks)).Split(%27;%27)[0])'">
    <!-- Since DuckDB 2.0 a release ships the shared libraries as duckdb-shared-libs-<platform>.tar.gz, as the nightly
         builds do, instead of libduckdb-<platform>.zip. A nightly build downloads only the platform it runs on. -->
    <ItemGroup Condition="'$(NightlyBuild)' != 'true'">
      <_NativeLib Include="win-x64" LibUrl="$(DuckDbArtifactRoot)/duckdb-shared-libs-windows-amd64.tar.gz" />
      <_NativeLib Include="win-arm64" LibUrl="$(DuckDbArtifactRoot)/duckdb-shared-libs-windows-arm64.tar.gz" />
      <_NativeLib Include="linux-x64" LibUrl="$(DuckDbArtifactRoot)/duckdb-shared-libs-linux-amd64.tar.gz" />
      <_NativeLib Include="linux-arm64" LibUrl="$(DuckDbArtifactRoot)/duckdb-shared-libs-linux-arm64.tar.gz" />
      <_NativeLib Include="osx" LibUrl="$(DuckDbArtifactRoot)/duckdb-shared-libs-osx-universal.tar.gz" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <ItemGroup Condition="'$(NightlyBuild)' == 'true'">
      <_NativeLib Include="win-x64" LibUrl="$(DuckDbArtifactRoot)/duckdb-shared-libs-windows-amd64.tar.gz" Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Windows'))" />
      <_NativeLib Include="linux-x64" LibUrl="$(DuckDbArtifactRoot)/duckdb-shared-libs-linux-amd64.tar.gz" Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Linux'))" />
      <_NativeLib Include="osx" LibUrl="$(DuckDbArtifactRoot)/duckdb-shared-libs-osx-universal.tar.gz" Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('OSX'))" />
    </ItemGroup>
    <MSBuild Projects="DownloadNativeLibs.targets" Properties="Rid=%(_NativeLib.Identity);LibUrl=%(_NativeLib.LibUrl)" />
  </Target>
  <Target Name="CleanNativeLibs" BeforeTargets="Clean" Condition="'$(BuildType)' == 'Full' ">
    <RemoveDir Directories="obj\runtimes" />
  </Target>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(BuildType)' == 'Full' ">
    <None Include="obj\runtimes\**\*.dll;obj\runtimes\**\*.so;obj\runtimes\**\*.dylib;">
      <Visible>false</Visible>
      <CopyToOutputDirectory>PreserveNewest</CopyToOutputDirectory>
      <Pack>true</Pack>
      <PackagePath>\runtimes</PackagePath>
      <Link>runtimes\%(RecursiveDir)\%(FileName)%(Extension)</Link>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">
    <PackageReference Include="GitVersion.MsBuild" Version="6.4.0" PrivateAssets="all" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <!-- End native lib section -->

  <!-- The bindings of the C API V2 are internal until DuckDB marks V2 stable (docs/V2-MIGRATION.md). -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="DuckDB.NET.Data, " />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="DuckDB.NET.Test, " />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
